Demonstrative_Examples.Demonstrative_Example[0].Intro_Text: Many SoCs use hardware to partition system resources between trusted and untrusted entities. One example of this concept is the Arm TrustZone, in which the processor and all security-aware IP attempt to isolate resources based on the status of a privilege bit. This privilege bit is part of the input interface in all TrustZone-aware IP. If this privilege bit is accidentally grounded or left unconnected when the IP is instantiated, privilege escalation of all input data may occur.
